./notes/MATHEMATICA_MIRROR_POLICY.md:48:IV.x/V.1 integrity remediation, batch 2 (2026-05-29) re-verified four more stages (105, 106, 109, 112) whose first-pass IV.2 fixes had been applied orchestrator-direct (Codex bypassed); three of the closed findings added GENUINE independent second-engine routes (NOT accepted policy mirrors), and `material_change: false` on every stage. **105 F1** (checkpoint) — the `.wl` chi_Q derivation was rewritten along an independent residue/`Reduce`-witness path: a single-ratio retarded module, an `Im[]` projection of the odd-frequency channel, and operator-product polynomial inversion, with non-transliterated names; this is genuine cross-engine independence against the SymPy companion, not a policy mirror. 9 Mathematica PASS. **106 F3** — the `.wl` was re-authored on an independent `Yret` one-pole omega-series path that derives chi_Q=1 directly from the ω⁵ match (distinct from the SymPy route); 11 Mathematica PASS. **112 F2** — added an independent Stage-92 linearized `(b, a0, a5) = (0, 3σ, −σγ)` cross-check that derives `gamma_W = 1/9` alongside the existing chi_Q route; the `.py` lacks this Stage-92 route, so the two engines now use structurally different derivations of the same constant. 14 Mathematica PASS. (109's closed findings were `tautological_check`/`paper_misalignment`, not `mathematica_transliteration` — its `.wl` was nonetheless re-derived via separate num/den linearization + denominator series-inversion, independent of the `.py`'s direct-ratio path; the `coeff=(chiSeries-1)/eps` intermediate was removed.) Previous batch-1 entry below.
./notes/MATHEMATICA_MIRROR_POLICY.md:62:IV.2 audit (2026-05-27) caught `mathematica_transliteration` patterns on 5 of 7 dirty stages (105 — full `.wl` rewrite with structurally distinct path: unfactored ratio + `Apart` round-trip check + `SeriesCoefficient` operator form + `Reduce`-over-reals for chi_Q + polynomial inversion of `Λ·Y = -3` for the deformed branch; variable names changed (no `yRet`/`lamDef`/`yDef`/`omegaQ`/`sigmaCan`). 106 — full `.wl` re-author starting from the retarded one-pole form `Y_ret(omega) = 3/4 + (1/4)/(1 - omega^2/OmegaQ^2 - i chi_Q sigma_Q^can omega^5)`, series-expanding to omega^7 to show next odd term is at O(omega^7), with no `nqGeneral`/`k0`/`k2`/`k4`/`gamma5` intermediates; closure to N_Q=1 via source-map relation. 109 — linearization rewrite via numerator/denominator-separate series + `Series[1/denominator]` inversion + multiply, solving `chiSeries - 1 == 0` directly for `a5` without the `coeff = (chiSeries - 1)/eps` intermediate. 111 — added independent chi_Q^mix re-derivation block bypassing the L0/L5 extraction (geometric-series form of the pole alone), plus new `expectZero["chi_Q^mix routes agree", chiMix - chiMixAlt]`. 112 — added independent Stage-92 linearized cross-check extracting `(a_0, a_5) = (3 sigma, -sigma gamma)` from solB's deformation and solving the preservation condition `a_0/3 + 9 a_5 = 0` for `gamma_W = 1/9`, an algebraically distinct route from the chi_Q-based solve). Transliteration share for IV.2 = 5/7 = 71% dirty; higher than IV.1 (4/11 = 36%) but several of these were borderline mathematical mirrors where the structural rewrite added genuine engine independence rather than pure renaming. **No new pitfall candidates** from IV.2 — all orchestrator-direct edits applied first-attempt clean. But pitfall #11 (PASS-line discipline) was **re-confirmed prominently**: 108 F2 caught `chiArg /. beta -> 1 - 1` parsing as `(chiArg /. (beta -> 0))` because Mathematica `Plus`/`Subtract` binds tighter than `Rule`. The buggy assertion `0^5 = 0` had been silently passing on every prior run; only the auditor's structural read caught it. Fix: `(chiArg /. beta -> 1) - 1`. This is a **persistent class of silent-pass bug** — any directive instructing Codex to write `expr /. var -> value <op> rest` must use explicit parentheses around the `Rule`, or the parser bends the bracket. Augment pitfall #11 with: Mathematica `/.` (ReplaceAll) binds looser than `+`/`-`/`*`/`/`/`^` but Rule binds even looser; always parenthesize `(expr /. rule)` when followed by arithmetic.
./notes/MATHEMATICA_MIRROR_POLICY.md:64:IV.1 audit (2026-05-27) caught `mathematica_transliteration` patterns on 4 of 11 dirty stages (091 — full series+Solve+assertions port; closed with an independent partial-fraction recombination block using `Together` not `Series`. 092 — full Series+Solve[branch==0, kg0] port; closed with a restructure to work in dimensionless `(eps_2, eps_4)` variables from the outset, deriving `K_0 = 4 K_2^2/K_4` directly without `Solve[]`. 095 — line-by-line Schur-complement port; closed with an independent Schur derivation block via `Solve[D[Lq, gSym] == 0, gSym]` from the bilinear L action, before the existing series machinery. 097 — line-by-line algebraic choreography port; closed with an independent route via `SeriesCoefficient[kbarCons[w], {w, 0, n}]` series extraction rather than direct definitions, and `gamma5Target` derived via `9 k0Target/(32 omegaQ^5)` not `9 k2Target^(5/2)/k0Target^(3/2)`). **100 F4 (`mathematica_transliteration` for the outgoing-normalization series choreography) was marked BLOCKED in the directive as a design-level rewrite needing user direction; user picked Cluster B (c) which strengthens the substantive closure derivation but does not authorize a full second-engine rewrite. 100's load-bearing closure assertion is now non-tautological on both engines (`mhat_0^2 Gamma_5 = Gamma_5_target` imposed as the observable condition, derives `mhat_0^2 chi_Q N_Q = 1`), but the upstream series-expansion choreography still follows SymPy step-for-step.** Transliteration share for IV.1 = 4/11 = 36% dirty; lower than III.3 (4/7 = 57%) but higher than III.5 (3/5 = 60% with 1 won't-fix). **No new pitfall candidates from IV.1** — all orchestrator-direct edits applied first-attempt clean; verifier PASS-line counting confirmed expected substantive checks across all 12 stages (e.g., 094 Mathematica 34 PASS lines = 30 orthogonality + 1 Y00 norm + 3 static-limit; 097 Mathematica 9 PASS = 2 series-equiv + 1 Gamma5 closed form + 1 geometric target + 1 Gamma5_target + 4 R_i).
