./notes/PAPER_CLEANUP_TRACKER.md:636:| P5-11 | Pass-2 Batch IV.2 — ZERO paper/notes edits; 4 script-side `.wl` fixes (105 checkpoint DtN-fingerprint de-tautologization + 107/110/114 transliteration re-authors, all user-authorized independent routes); + 1 deferred stale-review-artifact residual (`stage_103_review.md` reviews Stage 035) for later cleanup | verification | done (edit); 1 residual DEFERRED | 2026-06-06: Pass-2 Batch IV.2 (103-114, `Part IV.2 — Outgoing DtN, deformation, robustness, robin`), 12/12 re-verified at v2 depth + value-reconciliation augmentation (**86 deliverable values checked batch-wide, 0 misaligned** — 104=11, 105=8, 106=11, 107=9, 108=14, 109=4, 110=6, 111=9, 112=7, 114=7, plus status-only 103 [symbolic carry-forward] and 113 [8 notes-stated] reconciled), `material_change: false` on all 12 → NO downstream staling, 0 Codex deviations, all iter-1 exit 0. **ZERO paper/`.tex`/notes-stage edits this batch** — no genuine `paper_misalignment` anywhere (no value dispute, no user value-gate triggered). TWO checkpoints in range (**105** owns `chi_Q=1`; **112** owns `gamma_W=1/9`) — BOTH cleared the higher bar, NO checkpoint constant moved, no new pinned constant. NO EM-projected stages, no new postulated constants. **103 and 113 are status-only** (no scripts). All source changes are SCRIPTS (no prose), all four `.wl`-only: **105** (CHECKPOINT) F1 `insufficient_verification` (+ an F2 `mathematica_transliteration` audit OVER-CALL — the retarded half was already independent) — both engines had matched the canonical ω⁵ coefficient to a HARDCODED fingerprint target `a^5/(27 c_s^5)` (= `sigma_can/4` retyped), never evaluating the actual outgoing l=2 Hankel DtN; DE-TAUTOLOGIZED (Claude+Codex math-coverage, non-conceptual, user-informed) — both engines now DERIVE `Lambda_2^out = z d/dz ln h_2^(1)(z)` via VISIBLY DISTINCT constructions (SymPy `j_2 + i*y_2` closed form vs Mathematica native `SphericalHankelH1[2,z]`), assert the can-fail series `-3 + z²/3 + z⁴