paper/appendices/stage_ledger.tex:269:\hyperref[stage:100]{100} & IV & \resultanchor{MTDC-T8} & \StatusExactClosure{} & \textbf{Factorized \(2.5\)PN defect.} Full odd normalization factorizes as \(\widehat m_0^{\,2}\chi_Q N_Q=1\). \\
paper/appendices/stage_ledger.tex:271:\hyperref[stage:101]{101} & IV & \resultanchor{MTDC-T8} & \StatusReduced{} / \StatusExactClosure{} & \textbf{Natural source-map reduction.} On the natural point-particle source map, \(\widehat m_0\to1\), so the last obstruction is purely \(\chi_Q\). \\
paper/appendices/stage_ledger.tex:275:\hyperref[stage:103]{103} & IV & \resultanchor{MTDC-T8} & \StatusExactClosure{} / \StatusOpen{} & \textbf{Conditional reduced \(2.5\)PN closure.} Reduced theorem closes iff the actual passive/outgoing branch has \(\chi_Q=1\). \\
paper/appendices/stage_ledger.tex:277:\hyperref[stage:104]{104} & IV & \resultanchor{MTDC-T8} & \StatusExactClosure{} & \textbf{Exact outgoing \(l=2\) DtN fingerprint.} Spherical Hankel DtN expansion gives \(\widehat Y_2^{\rm out}=1+z^2/9+4z^4/81+iz^5/27+\cdots\). \\
paper/appendices/stage_ledger.tex:279:\hyperref[stage:105]{105} & IV & \resultanchor{MTDC-T8} & \StatusExactClosure{} & \textbf{Exact fixing of \(\chi_Q\).} Matching the canonical grouped module to the exact outgoing DtN branch gives \(\chi_Q=1\). \\
paper/appendices/stage_ledger.tex:283:\hyperref[stage:107]{107} & IV & \resultanchor{MTDC-T8} & \StatusExactClosure{} & \textbf{General isotropic DtN deformation algebra.} Deformed branch \(S\Lambda_2^{\rm out}(\beta z)+\Sigma_0+\Sigma_2z^2+\Sigma_4z^4+i\Sigma_5z^5\) gives explicit \(\chi_Q\). \\
paper/appendices/stage_ledger.tex:285:\hyperref[stage:108]{108} & IV & \resultanchor{MTDC-T8} & \StatusExactClosure{} & \textbf{Robustness classes for \(\chi_Q\).} Pure scale is harmless; pure argument shift is harmless only if even moments remain canonical; additive throat-core data can move \(\chi_Q\). \\
paper/appendices/stage_ledger.tex:289:\hyperref[stage:110]{110} & IV & \resultanchor{MTDC-T8} & \StatusExactClosure{} & \textbf{Isotropic Robin outlet.} Pure Robin shift gives \(\chi_Q^{\rm R}=3/(3-\rho_R)\) and generically spoils the branch. \\
paper/appendices/stage_ledger.tex:457:\hyperref[stage:194]{194} & V & \resultanchor{MTDC-T9} & \StatusExactClosure{} & \textbf{Outgoing \(l=2\) fingerprint.} Derives the exact outgoing spherical DtN fingerprint and fixes \(\chi_Q=1\) on the canonical compact branch. \\
paper/appendices/stage_ledger.tex:459:\hyperref[stage:195]{195} & V & \resultanchor{MTDC-T9} & \StatusExactClosure{} / \StatusReduced{} & \textbf{Source-map reduction.} Factorizes the observable odd closure as \(\widehat m_0^{2}\chi_QN_Q=1\) and collapses \(\Delta_{\rm norm}\). \\
paper/appendices/stage_ledger.tex:463:\hyperref[stage:197]{197} & V & \resultanchor{MTDC-T9} & \StatusExactClosure{} & \textbf{Conditional Packet-A closure.} Proves \(\Delta_{\rm branch}=0\iff \chi_Q=1\) and hence \(\Delta_Q=\chi_Q-1\) is the sole Packet-A scalar. \\
paper/appendices/stage_ledger.tex:475:\hyperref[stage:203]{203} & VI & \resultanchor{MTDC-T10} & \StatusExactClosure{} & \textbf{Scalar graph-slice theorem.} Reduces graph-aligned realization to the single scalar \(\widehat\chi_Q(\mathbf y)=1\), proves graph tangency to \(\ker M_*\), and gives the one-parameter crossing theorem. \\
