./redteam/pass2/batches/batch_IV2.md:12:- **105 (CHECKPOINT — higher bar) — F1 `insufficient_verification` + F2 `mathematica_transliteration`:** The `chi_Q=1` pin was tautological — BOTH engines matched the canonical ω⁵ coefficient against a HARDCODED fingerprint target `a^5/(27 c_s^5)` (= `sigma_can/4` retyped), never evaluating the actual outgoing l=2 Hankel DtN fingerprint. F2 was an OVER-CALL by the audit agent: the `.wl` retarded half already used `Im[]`-projection + `Reduce`/`ToRules` + a factored form and the deformed branch was independent — but it SHARED the hardcoded-RHS tautology. **DE-TAUTOLOGIZED (Claude+Codex math-coverage, non-conceptual, user-informed):** both engines now DERIVE `Lambda_2^out = z d/dz ln h_2^(1)(z)` from the spherical Hankel function via VISIBLY DISTINCT constructions — SymPy from an explicit `j_2 + i*y_2` (spherical Bessel) closed form, Mathematica from native `SphericalHankelH1[2,z]` — assert the can-fail fingerprint series `= -3 + z²/3 + z⁴/9 + i z⁵/9`, read the DERIVED `Y_2^out` imag z⁵ coefficient (`= 1/27`), and force `chi_Q=1` by matching the retarded ω⁵ coefficient to that DERIVED target (no typed literal on the RHS). `chi_Q=1` UNCHANGED; output only ADDED the fingerprint lines. F2 dissolves under the distinct per-engine constructions. **Cleared the checkpoint higher bar.** (Provenance: the 2026-05-29 integrity-remediation batch-2 had re-authored 105's `.wl` to a residue/`Reduce` path, but the verification-strength tautology in the hardcoded RHS survived in BOTH engines until pass-2 caught it.)
./redteam/pass2/batches/batch_IV2.md:13:- **107 — F1 `mathematica_transliteration` (pass-1 MISSED):** the `.wl` was a full line-by-line port — `Series[l0/lambdaDef,{z,0,5}]` on the same normalized ratio as the `.py`, identical `lambdaDef`/`l0/l2/l4/l5`/`yFormula`/`Solve` order. **USER-AUTHORIZED RE-AUTHOR:** the `.wl` now reaches the deformed branch / `chi_Q` via an order-by-order undetermined-coefficient solve of the operator identity `Lambda_def*Y = L0` (`CoefficientList` + `Solve`, unique-solution guard); all `Series`/`series` removed. Independent (verify-confirmed). MMA output byte-identical. (The 2026-05-27 IV.2 audit fixed 105/106/109/111/112's `.wl` but not 107; never a sanctioned mirror, so the re-author reverses no pass-1 disposition.)
./redteam/pass2/batches/batch_IV2.md:18:- **105** cleared the higher bar — `chi_Q=1` now forced by the derived Hankel fingerprint, no longer self-matched against a typed literal. Owns `chi_Q=1`.
