    10	  (iii) "minimal-module hypothesis on any support/source success statement"
    11	are upstream carry-ins from Part III + IV.1 stages:
    12	  (i)  derives from stage 091 (grouped P2 + static geometry) and stage 092
    13	       (dynamic-geometry obstruction); reduction is asserted explicitly at
    14	       stage 094 (after orthogonality) and stage 096 (verdict).
    15	  (ii) is the full content of stage 094 (15 angular integrals + Laplace
    16	       eigenvalue) in both engines.
    17	  (iii) is anchored by the Part III chain stages 088 / 089 / 090.
    18	This stage uses those upstream outputs without re-deriving them.
    19	"""
    20	from __future__ import annotations
    21	import sympy as sp
    22	
    23	G, c, c_s, a = sp.symbols('G c c_s a', positive=True, real=True)
    24	K0, Omega = sp.symbols('K0 Omega', positive=True, real=True)
    25	
    26	# Actual branch conservative module coefficients.
    27	K2 = sp.simplify(K0 / (4 * Omega**2))
    28	K4 = sp.simplify(K0 / (4 * Omega**4))
    29	Gamma5 = sp.simplify(9 * K2**sp.Rational(5, 2) / K0**sp.Rational(3, 2))
    30	Gamma5_expected = sp.simplify(9 * K0 / (32 * Omega**5))
    31	assert sp.simplify(Gamma5 - Gamma5_expected) == 0
    32	
    33	# GR target normalization.
    34	K0_target = sp.simplify(64 * G * Omega**5 / (45 * c**5))
